// Chapter 1 — the camp. Shows a hub (@hub) whose options are storylets tagged "camp".

=== camp.arrival
@title Base Camp

![A clearing at the jungle's edge, tents sagging in the heat](camp-art)

The boat leaves {player:first-name} at the edge of the jungle with a pack, a {item:torch#lower} and
three weeks of unanswered letters. The {faction:explorers-guild:name} has given {player:pronoun#object}
one season to find the **Relic of Ysh** before they hand the expedition to someone more *reliable*.

> guide: {player:first-name} {player:last-name}. You're later than your letter promised. I'm Tomas — the guild sent me.

{player:last-name#possessive} reputation for punctuality is, {player:pronoun} has to admit, deserved.

-> camp.hub

=== camp.hub
@title The Camp
@hub camp

The camp hums with insects. Tomas sharpens a machete by the fire{if var:supplies > 0}, eyeing the supplies
you bought{/if}.

* [Set out for the temple] -> trail.river
* [Visit the expedition workshop] -> workshop.hub
* [Try the field exercises] -> field.hub

=== camp.supplies
@title Haggle for supplies
@tags camp
@once

A trader with a gold tooth unrolls a blanket of goods. You come away with a {item:rope#lower} and a
{item:charm#lower} he swears keeps the river spirits polite.

~ give player rope
~ give player charm
~ var:supplies += 2
-> camp.hub

=== camp.guide
@title Ask Tomas about the temple
@tags camp
@once

> guide: The old ones built it to keep something *in*, not people out. The guild knows that. They never write it down.

Tomas tells you about the river crossing, and about the explorer who went in last spring and came out
talking only in numbers.

{if faction:explorers-guild >= friendly}
> guide: The guild speaks well of you. I'll do what I can.
{else}
> guide: Between us, the guild expects you to fail.
{/if}

~ faction:explorers-guild += 5
-> camp.hub

=== camp.journal
@title Study your journal
@tags camp
@once
@priority 5

You spread {player:pronoun#possessive} field journal across your knees. The glyph rubbings from the museum
are smudged, but a pattern repeats: *a spiral, a closed eye, a hand.*

* [Puzzle out the glyphs] skill-check history dc 12
  success: { set flag:knows-glyphs; player:xp += 50 } -> camp.journal-solved
  failure: -> camp.journal-failed

=== camp.journal-solved
It's a warning and an instruction at once: *close your eyes before the spiral, and the hand will open the way.*
You underline it twice.
-> camp.hub

=== camp.journal-failed
The marks blur into each other. You close the journal with a headache and nothing else.
-> camp.hub
